{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting","id":158482,"title":"Who are the Sidereals without the Setting?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-03T18:18:59-07:00","id":158482,"title":"Who are the Sidereals without the Setting?","content":"This concept got brought up in a different thread and I wanted to explore it more fully without derailing the previous discussion.<br /> <br /> The concept is what happens to the sidereal splat if you remove Yu-Shan, contact with the Pattern Spiders and all of the Heaven based business and guidelines from the sidereal concept. Essentially not much is left for a Sidereal to be a Sidereal (as opposed to any other kind of exalt).<br /> <br /> If you look at Solars with &quot;setting support&quot; then you have the First Age, without that support structure and their tendency to rule, you have the classic second age solar. Both are recognizable as Solar Exalts, with solar powers and doing solar things.<br /> <br /> Lunars have pretty much the same result. They are transhumanist shape shifters of animalistic qualities regardless if they are city socialites, building a private society away from civilization, being shape shifting elite scouts for a first age solar army or just being the Exalted analog to the shifters of Werewolf the Apocalypse game. Alchemicals fall under similar transhumanist genre concepts.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded follow the same path in that their powers are inherited, which makes any story permutation based around family automatically in their domain. With setting support you have the Realm or Lookshy or the First Age Gentes. Without setting support you have the classic lost egg games where they play the wandering heroes trying to carve out a niche for themselves which is found in almost every fantasy rpg.<br /> <br /> While occasionally poorly implemented, even Abyssals function regardless of setup. They can have setting support by being loyalists who follow their patron deathlords orders or they can for go it and try to be tragic heroes who constantly struggles to overcome their condition and attempt redemption. Regardless which path they choose death in all its forms and permutations are never far behind them.<br /> <br /> Now lets look at the Sidereals...... without their plot device setup as running a chunk of heaven, without benefit of there being a comparatively large number of elder essence Sidereals running around, without access to the pattern spiders to wield astrology, without benefit of advanced martial arts.... what exactly are the sidereals?<br /> <br /> If say you swap the sidereal character generation with say a Solar or Lunar and restrict the backgrounds accordingly, there isn't very much &quot;sidereal-ness&quot; left in a sidereal. In fact if you consider just how much of their charm set would not be worth taking since they wouldn't be working for heaven or running related missions, one could be forgiven for considering their charm set under developed.<br /> <br /> If you think about it, Sidereals don't serve a clear function in an Army of any sort (unlike Solars, Lunars or Dragon-Blooded), they don't have the forced character oversight that say the Infernals do despite being clearly chosen by very powerful beings that are active in the running of Creation, they are not allowed to be active heroes who are known for their exploits even if they are in service to others like what the Alchemicals do.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T18:42:42-07:00","id":158510,"title":"","content":"Sidereals are advisors, counselors, sifus, viziers. So long as an army has a leader, that leader will need strategists and tacticians to advise her.<br /> <br /> One would assume that whatever setting you transplant Sidereals into, their weird fate powers still work somehow, even without a Loom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T18:47:16-07:00","id":158518,"title":"","content":"My interpretation of Sidereals (and/or how I would do them if it were up to me): Fate-ninjas fixing glitches in the Matrix - they are the only ones with the powerset and gadgets necessary to sew the fabric of reality back together (or exploit it and it's fraying edges). Even without the setting, fate (as opposed to Fate) is still / can still be a thing conceptually, and glitches in reality can still happen for whatever reason. I'd see them similar to Agents (Matrix again); or maybe even demons in Demon: The Descent, mixed with The Adjustment Bureau shenanigans (if you only keep the actually interesting bits).<br /> <br /> Although...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting#post158482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If say you swap the sidereal character generation with say a Solar or Lunar and restrict the backgrounds accordingly, there isn't very much &quot;sidereal-ness&quot; left in a sidereal. In fact if you consider just how much of their charm set would not be worth taking since they wouldn't be working for heaven or running related missions, one could be forgiven for considering their charm set under developed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree that not working for heaven makes their charmset useless - you can still move cities around, give your pet dog magical powers or turn it into a dragon, give your drunkenness to other people, rearrange the landscape to your liking, be completely unable to die from any amount of physical damage (for a while anyway) and travel 6400 miles in 5 minutes because you simply <i>must not be late</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T18:52:38-07:00","id":158523,"title":"","content":"Sidereals without the whole heavenly aspect of Yu-Shan and Loom of Fate? This is where they get a little bit weak. The reason is that they were designed with that in mind. Without it, they are still mysterious ninja and assassins who show up at the the exact worst time and disappear at will. They still make great advisors, and they make a great conspiracy of elders who never take direct action. Part of the problem is I never really saw them as the front line hero, but the movers and shakers in the background.<br /> <br /> I think what you are doing is a little unfair, as their first age and second age rolls are very different, and you are removing the second age roll from them in many ways. Without access to heaven, Martial Arts, Astrology, Pattern Spiders, and heaven, well yeah, there's not much left. Even many (at least some) of their charms reference heaven or pattern spiders, like Efficient Secretary Technique. So yes, without most of their powers, they aren't very interesting. <br /> <br /> You can do them as Ronin, agents of heaven who never go there, secret identity superhero ninjas (that guy who runs that shop that isn't very interesting who is never around when monsters attack, MI-6 type adventures, old school Mission Impossible stuff, but they do lose a lot of character.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T18:56:58-07:00","id":158524,"title":"","content":"This is where a long view on the line is beneficial: all the stuff you're saying Sidereals are incoherent and redundant without is stuff that was introduced more than two years into the game line. Without that, you're left with the things that led people to think Sidereals were cool in the first place: they're mysterious, esoteric exalted with uncanny foresight and an intimate connection to spirits and destiny (not the Loom of Fate, which didn't exist, but &quot;destiny&quot; in a general sense), who practice powerful martial arts: heroes destined from birth to be peerless advisors and teachers, but who seized autonomy for themselves long ago in the doubt that others could be trusted to lead.<br /> <br /> Before the Sidereals book came out, the main concern was &quot;how the hell are they going to make these guys a playable faction?&quot;, not &quot;I don't see why these guys are in the game.&quot; On the contrary, it's always been the Lunars who didn't really have a clear role in the history of the setting -- they were largely redundant with the Solar Night Caste in the Primordial War and First Age. And while the Sidereals book threw in a ton of new shit out of left field, it left their core themes undisturbed, which is to say that their niche -- which was very firmly established straight out of the core -- was not changed, just greatly embellished upon.<br /> <br /> That said, there is one thing from the hardback that's a huge part of the modern &quot;Sidereal thing&quot;, but which you're passing over, and that's their charmset. The Sidereal charmset encodes a very large amount of the Sidereal thematics, in ways both overt and subtle. Some of their charms are wired into the Heaven/Loom motif, but that's just a loose rationalization, so they'd probably still have those charms if you removed Sidereal Astrology and all the hardback fluff. It's not an exaggeration to say that, until Infernals was published near the very end of the line, there had never been anything in the history of Exalted whose essence was as deeply encoded into its charmset as the Sidereals. If you don't make an attempt to understand the information about them contained in the charms, you aren't really going to get what their deal is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 06-03-2014, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T18:58:11-07:00","id":158526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korhal_IV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=158510#post158510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals are advisors, counselors, sifus, viziers. So long as an army has a leader, that leader will need strategists and tacticians to advise her.<br /> <br /> One would assume that whatever setting you transplant Sidereals into, their weird fate powers still work somehow, even without a Loom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think for the purposes of a game that is probably the best way to handle things. You just need to find a way to may the tools a sidereal has access to intrinsic to them rather than a greater force or organisation, or substitute the Loom and Yu-Shan for some other powerful bodies fitting with your setting.<br /> <br /> Tangent...<br /> <br /> This has got me thinking, if you opened a portal from Creation to the real world, and a exalt stepped through, would they still be a exalt? Could powers fueled by essence work in the long term in a world where there was no essence to respire? For that matter how would motes of essence (the building blocks of everything in creation) interact with atoms and other particles in the real world. Could a Solar respire the photons and radiations which bombards the earth each day in the form of sunlight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T19:48:11-07:00","id":158582,"title":"","content":"No, which we should be thankful for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T20:03:48-07:00","id":158607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=158526#post158526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has got me thinking, if you opened a portal from Creation to the real world, and a exalt stepped through, would they still be a exalt? Could powers fueled by essence work in the long term in a world where there was no essence to respire? For that matter how would motes of essence (the building blocks of everything in creation) interact with atoms and other particles in the real world. Could a Solar respire the photons and radiations which bombards the earth each day in the form of sunlight?</div> </div> </div> </div>easy, the atoms are made of essence, we just dont have a way to see it as that, we respire essence and all that but have no way to use it like Creation does, in exchange we have electricity and wi fi.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1351,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","user":"Sakii","date":". 06-03-2014, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T20:21:08-07:00","id":158616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting#post158482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This concept got brought up in a different thread and I wanted to explore it more fully without derailing the previous discussion.<br /> <br /> The concept is what happens to the sidereal splat if you remove Yu-Shan, contact with the Pattern Spiders and all of the Heaven based business and guidelines from the sidereal concept. Essentially not much is left for a Sidereal to be a Sidereal (as opposed to any other kind of exalt).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually played in two games like this!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you look at Solars with &quot;setting support&quot; then you have the First Age, without that support structure and their tendency to rule, you have the classic second age solar. Both are recognizable as Solar Exalts, with solar powers and doing solar things. </div> </div> </div>That seems debatable. I know a lot of people who thought that the whole problem with the First Age was the <i>lack</i> of Solar things to do. Being Eternal Glorious King #146 put some people off the whole thing, in fact.<br /> <br /> (Note: I'm not endorsing that interpretation, but it seems less than totally clear-cut)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lunars have pretty much the same result. They are transhumanist shape shifters of animalistic qualities regardless if they are city socialites, building a private society away from civilization, being shape shifting elite scouts for a first age solar army or just being the Exalted analog to the shifters of Werewolf the Apocalypse game. Alchemicals fall under similar transhumanist genre concepts. </div> </div> </div>Very good!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dragon-Blooded follow the same path in that their powers are inherited, which makes any story permutation based around family automatically in their domain. With setting support you have the Realm or Lookshy or the First Age Gentes. Without setting support you have the classic lost egg games where they play the wandering heroes trying to carve out a niche for themselves which is found in almost every fantasy rpg. </div> </div> </div>It's good to have multiple modes of play, although I even know some players who would consider the distinction between a Lost Egg game and a proper Dynastic power squabble to be larger than the difference between playing some other splats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While occasionally poorly implemented, even Abyssals function regardless of setup. They can have setting support by being loyalists who follow their patron deathlords orders or they can for go it and try to be tragic heroes who constantly struggles to overcome their condition and attempt redemption. Regardless which path they choose death in all its forms and permutations are never far behind them. </div> </div> </div>Alright.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now lets look at the Sidereals...... without their plot device setup as running a chunk of heaven, without benefit of there being a comparatively large number of elder essence Sidereals running around, without access to the pattern spiders to wield astrology, without benefit of advanced martial arts.... what exactly are the sidereals? </div> </div> </div>You need more detail than that. Are you assuming a setting in which Sidereals are tossed into the world without direction like the archetypical Solar game? No Arcane Fate? ...no political consequences for re-arranging mountains? Then you quickly end up with characters who are much more powerful and focused on ground-level events than I think you're anticipating. <br /> <br /> Now, if you think that seems like a bit of a lackluster concept... that's probably because it would be the absolute most vanilla background any Exalt has, bar none. Even the Solars and Lunars are commonly-defined by their pasts, by a world in which they are hunted. It seems unfair to put a Sidereal Exalt in a huge white room and say 'Seems bland'.<br /> <br /> But I've played games like that, and the fix was easy. Sidereal prophecy and visions are baked right into the charmset from Ess 1- all you have to do is emphasize those, give Sidereals a brief history and something to do in general (in our case, it was to follow visions gathering the resources of a scattered Creation to fight big bads, but that's hardly the only possible solution). Suddenly they have relevance and motive again!<br /> <br /> (Also, I'm not sure why they wouldn't have advanced martial arts. At this stage that's kinda baked into the mechanics of the splat.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If say you swap the sidereal character generation with say a Solar or Lunar and restrict the backgrounds accordingly, there isn't very much &quot;sidereal-ness&quot; left in a sidereal. In fact if you consider just how much of their charm set would not be worth taking since they wouldn't be working for heaven or running related missions, one could be forgiven for considering their charm set under developed. </div> </div> </div>Look, I'm not much for combat. It's totally possible that what you're saying is right on that level.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I've played Sidereals who were nigh-unkillable, Sidereals who could cross Creation in a day, Sidereals who could bind major gods with a word, Sidereals who could doom a kingdom at a glance and Sidereals who could have stopped the march of a Realm Legion single-handedly. Frankly, I've always thought that if I weren't running missions for Heaven and burdened with divine oversight, my characters could seriously fuck up the current order.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you think about it, Sidereals don't serve a clear function in an Army of any sort (unlike Solars, Lunars or Dragon-Blooded), they don't have the forced character oversight that say the Infernals do despite being clearly chosen by very powerful beings that are active in the running of Creation, they are not allowed to be active heroes who are known for their exploits even if they are in service to others like what the Alchemicals do. </div> </div> </div>I'm not a general. I've never served in an army. I get trounced a lot in Civilization, frankly. What I'm saying is that I could be totally mistaken about this, but having tacticians who can <i>see the future</i> is probably something of a moderate boon to a commander.* Now, I grant you that 'tactician' doesn't usually include things like the ability to rescue the entire command core from sure death, infalliably sense assassins, re-arrange the geography or transmit your entire army into the enemy's command post- but I think those are worthwhile bonuses for an advisor to bring to the table.<br /> <br /> It's certainly true that making a Sidereal who is a great and beloved hero throughout the kingdom is pretty hard, but that's generally accepted as an intentional thematic.<br /> <br /> I'm just not seeing it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *The counterargument here, of course, is that the Primordials are or should be immune to such predictions. Well, they aren't actually immune to the bulk of Sidereal charms in that vein, but even if you think they really ought to be that doesn't make those charms useless throughout the whole of the War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T20:44:15-07:00","id":158628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=158524#post158524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is where a long view on the line is beneficial: all the stuff you're saying Sidereals are incoherent and redundant without is stuff that was introduced more than two years into the game line. Without that, you're left with the things that led people to think Sidereals were cool in the first place: they're mysterious, esoteric exalted with uncanny foresight and an intimate connection to spirits and destiny (not the Loom of Fate, which didn't exist, but &quot;destiny&quot; in a general sense), who practice powerful martial arts: heroes destined from birth to be peerless advisors and teachers, but who seized autonomy for themselves long ago in the doubt that others could be trusted to lead.<br /> <br /> Before the Sidereals book came out, the main concern was &quot;how the hell are they going to make these guys a playable faction?&quot;, not &quot;I don't see why these guys are in the game.&quot; On the contrary, it's always been the Lunars who didn't really have a clear role in the history of the setting -- they were largely redundant with the Solar Night Caste in the Primordial War and First Age. And while the Sidereals book threw in a ton of new shit out of left field, it left their core themes undisturbed, which is to say that their niche -- which was very firmly established straight out of the core -- was not changed, just greatly embellished upon.<br /> <br /> That said, there is one thing from the hardback that's a huge part of the modern &quot;Sidereal thing&quot;, but which you're passing over, and that's their charmset. The Sidereal charmset encodes a very large amount of the Sidereal thematics, in ways both overt and subtle. Some of their charms are wired into the Heaven/Loom motif, but that's just a loose rationalization, so they'd probably still have those charms if you removed Sidereal Astrology and all the hardback fluff. It's not an exaggeration to say that, until Infernals was published near the very end of the line, there had never been anything in the history of Exalted whose essence was as deeply encoded into its charmset as the Sidereals. If you don't make an attempt to understand the information about them contained in the charms, you aren't really going to get what their deal is.</div> </div> </div> </div>+1<br /> <br /> When Sidereals first came out myself and couple of my players were really taken aback because the book was a huge departure from what we envisioned Sidereals as. I'd like to see Sidereals in Yu-Shan taken out and replaced with Sidereals as the secret masters of Creation, running conspiracies, religions, and dojos across Creation from behind the scenes. Guiding their agents for their own reasons. Secret agents of Fate never really interested me that much. Besides the pattern spiders and Loom stuff are all just setting justifications for Sidereal destiny manipulation. Ditch them and just replace it with Sidereals reading destiny in the stars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T20:45:13-07:00","id":158631,"title":"","content":"I have often played games like this! More than once, even. Really, when you read the 1e corebook's description of Sidereals, you get an image of them, and then Exalted: the Sidereals gives you something else ENTIRELY... which is, you know, good and all. But without Heaven, they just focus on what IS actually their pitch: Being viziers, being manipulators behind the throne, spymasters of Creation. Heaven kind of detracts from it, as it makes being a power behind the throne kind of irrelevant, something that often annoys me.<br /> <br /> Also, it is important to mention that they don't need access to the Loom to use 99% of their powers. It is a very common mistake to believe that you need to be in the Loom to use Astrology. But they can do it anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T20:46:56-07:00","id":158632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=158607#post158607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> easy, the atoms are made of essence, we just dont have a way to see it as that, we respire essence and all that but have no way to use it like Creation does, in exchange we have electricity and wi fi.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sakii knows the true workings of the universe...he may be a Sidereal...further investigation required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T22:15:31-07:00","id":158716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=158632#post158632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sakii knows the true workings of the universe...he may be a Sidereal...further investigation required.</div> </div> </div> </div>in one week all traces of that post will be erased from the world anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T22:48:16-07:00","id":158743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting#post158482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The concept is what happens to the sidereal splat if you remove Yu-Shan, contact with the Pattern Spiders and all of the Heaven based business and guidelines from the sidereal concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>You get WoD 1.0 Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T01:38:13-07:00","id":158831,"title":"","content":"The Pattern Spiders are already just the mechanism for how Fate works, so &quot;removing&quot; them only means removing Astrology if one's alternate setting has no concept of or analogue to Fate at all, which seems an unfair handicap. Really, much as the whole scenario is; one is being exaggeratedly over-specific in their needs here, but to provide Sidereals without a concept of support structure is like... well, nothing for the other Exalted, since it's a distinguishing feature by design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T02:39:58-07:00","id":158856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting#post158482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">transhumanist</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, this thread was over <i>by the first post</i>.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\"><b>Warned for threadcrapping</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-05-2014, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T03:36:39-07:00","id":158877,"title":"","content":"Sidereals are still the secret masters secretly running everything behind the scenes with their secret powers of secretness.<br /> There are many, many settings and stories with a secret conspiracy of mysterious old guys who run everything, using their mysterious agents with strange powers. They don't have to live in Heaven to do so. Agent Smith stays in the Matrix the whole time, the Technocracy didn't run things from Horizon Realms most of the time, that's just where they did their experiments (and fought aliens). They operated on Earth.<br /> One could argue that the Sidereals work best as a secret conspiracy pulling the strings if it takes more work than asking your friendly local Celestial God &quot;so, who was behind the Usurpation? And they live where? And they are the Exalts of which Incarnae? Well that's interesting...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T04:18:05-07:00","id":158894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=158856#post158856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, this thread was over <i>by the first post</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's try and keep the shitposting to a minimum please. <br /> <br /> <br /> On the main topic, I've run games outside of Creation (World of Darkness cross overs, or custom settings). It's easy to take Solars, Lunars, Dragon Blooded and Abyssals and just drop them into different settings without too many changes. Even Infernals can be dropped into other settings to a degree, without feeling too much like fish out of water. <br /> <br /> Sidereal however are are tied to Creation, the Loom of Fate, the heavenly bureaucracy, and such, to the point that trying to use them without those elements causes them to lose a significant amount of what makes them interesting and cool. <br /> <br /> Alchemicals and Fair Folk run into similar issues, with Alchemicals being tied heavily to Autochthon and Fair Folk tied to the Wyld, that any attempt to drop them into settings use them in settings without those aspects can run into significant problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T05:19:03-07:00","id":158925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=158743#post158743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You get WoD 1.0 Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>People hugely overestimate the connection between Sidereals and mages, and I think it has more to do with their thinking tracing a narrative rut than due to anything fundamental about the splats.. They're only similar in a handful of ways, and those ways are mostly not large or significant to the character type. Sidereals have loose Easter-egg connections to oWod mages, but they are not &quot;the Exalted equivalent of oWoD mages&quot; (there isn't one), and approaching them from that angle is really misleading. The degree to which the two map to one another is so small that it doesn't provide much in the way of useful insight into either.<br /> <br /> Notice that oWoD mages have one of the most open, do-what-you-want power systems in any game ever, while Sidereals are defined in part by having the most restrictive power set of any major Exalted splat? Yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 06-04-2014, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T05:57:57-07:00","id":158946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=158894#post158894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereal however are are tied to Creation, the Loom of Fate, the heavenly bureaucracy, and such, to the point that trying to use them without those elements causes them to lose a significant amount of what makes them interesting and cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>How are they tied to Creation specifically?<br /> <br /> I mean, okay, if you put them in a setting where there are no spirits whatsoever, you're running into certain problems, since a good deal of their Charms interact with them (which is about the same as, say, wanting to run World of Darkness werewolves in a setting with no spirits).<br /> <br /> But even then, they've got a decent number of Charms that have nothing to do with spirits, and can easily have their method of function reworked to whatever setting. Their entire Presence cascade, off the top of my head. Maybe also Thrown?<br /> <br /> If anything, the Sidereals could actually do with a bit more to tie them into roles in the Celestial Order; as it is, if I think too hard on it, it starts feeling a little bit incidental.<br /> <br /> Not even Charms that specifically require them, just a sense that what Sidereals set out to do is significantly benefited from what is constituted by a support network of spirits; the problem of how nebulous the Sidereal oeuvre can feel has been brought up before.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I suppose if one wishes to preserve the Sidereal role of being necessary to the work for the continued existence of material reality, that's something that doesn't entirely transplant well between settings.<br /> <br /> But if they just need to be the Adjustment Bureau, jeez, just send them off with Presence in Absence Technique, Force Decision, Walking Outside Fate and Subordinate Inspiration Technique, and they're golden.<br /> <br /> Or they can be like a more diverse form of the Burn Legend Tennin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alchemicals and Fair Folk run into similar issues, with Alchemicals being tied heavily to Autochthon and Fair Folk tied to the Wyld, that any attempt to drop them into settings use them in settings without those aspects can run into significant problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd extend the question of exactly how proper it is to have Fair Folk with no odd Fairyland world, but admit that they could definitely use more of a sense of &quot;just&quot; being fearsome elfin figures, since so many of them should be at work in Creation proper as their particular experience of being exiled in the House of the Primordials.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T06:54:56-07:00","id":158982,"title":"","content":"Sidereal are tied heavily to the idea of the Loom of Fate and working to control destiny If you tried say, dropping them into (I don't know) some Forgotten Realms-esque setting, there's going to be some issues there because you'd <i>also</i> have to import the entire concept of Fate, Colleges, and all the other stuff that their mechanics key off of if you want the full &quot;Sidereal experience.&quot;<br /> <br /> Fair Folk are tied fairly heavily to the Wyld, so if you dropped them into a setting without something comparable to the Wyld, you'll again run into issues, though it's possible for them to skate by via harvesting gossamer from dreams and in 2.5 most of their charms work in Creation and the Wyld. Still, all of their Wyld-only charms would be totally useless in a setting without the Wyld.<br /> <br /> Alchemicals are tied to Autochthon in a fairly similar way (to the point that often times just bringing them into Creation proper raises certain issues) - they require taking their infrastructure with them. So if you bring Alchemicals into another setting, they'll also need to bring all of their steam-punk-magical-technology to create Vats, new charms, etc.<br /> <br /> Compare that to Solars or Abyssals or Dragon Blooded. You can drop them into pretty much any other setting, without worrying nearly as much that their mechanics are drawing on setting material unique to Creation.<br /> <br /> Basically Sidereal, Alchemicals and Fair Folk mechanics are heavily linked to setting-specific elements (Fate, Autochthon, and the Wyld respectively) that you would need to create analogues for those elements in your new setting, if you wanted them to retain the flavor that they are supposed to evoke.<br /> <br /> I mean, you <i>could</i> certainly make a setting without the concept of Fate, without colleges linked to specific star formations and have Sidereal without those elements, but you'll be cutting out a fair amount of their character and power. And the same is true for Fair Folk without the Wyld, or Alchemicals without their Vats and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-04-2014, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T07:56:06-07:00","id":159043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting#post158482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now let's look at the Sidereals...... without their plot device setup as running a chunk of heaven, without benefit of there being a comparatively large number of elder essence Sidereals running around, without access to the pattern spiders to wield astrology, without benefit of advanced martial arts.... what exactly are the sidereals?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) The pattern spiders do the drudge work for the Sidereals - it doesn't mean <b>you need them</b> to manipulate the Loom - MoEP: Sidereals makes a point of mentioning that, before there were the spiders, <b>the sidereals themselves along with the Maidens</b> were the ones responsible for the literal weaving of the tapestry of Fate for Creation. They are a majorly time-saving solution in tirerelessly caring for the drudge work, but that's what one would expect of essence constructs.<br /> <br /> Taking out the spiders, or even the Loom of Fate as some literal N/A artifact inside a mystic dome/sanctum in a different realm of existence, simply changes the <b>presentation</b> of the Sidereals role as oracle-viziers and agents of Fate - and <b>these</b> roles are most certainly thematic themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting#post158482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If say you swap the sidereal character generation with say a Solar or Lunar and restrict the backgrounds accordingly, there isn't very much &quot;sidereal-ness&quot; left in a sidereal. In fact if you consider just how much of their charm set would not be worth taking since they wouldn't be working for heaven or running related missions, one could be forgiven for considering their charm set under developed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because Yu-shan is<b> the only place in Creation</b> where a character <b>will deal with spirits &amp; fae, </b>care about <b>holes in reality</b> <b>that facilitate infiltration by demons, ghosts, fae &amp; less recognizable things</b> or <b>have use for precognitive charms</b>, ever, sure. Seriously, have you ever <b>actually used </b>a sidereal character in your games?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=158982#post158982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically Sidereal, Alchemicals and Fair Folk mechanics are heavily linked to setting-specific elements (Fate, Autochthon, and the Wyld respectively) that you would need to create analogues for those elements in your new setting, if you wanted them to retain the flavor that they are supposed to evoke.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other planes/other realms of existence? Seems like a pretty linear juxtaposition, actually. Not to mention Fate is all too easily connected with <b>Divination</b>, or the capacity to see patterns and the invisible world - neither of those things is particularly dependent on Exalted's setting. What makes Malfeas, the Wyld, the Underworld and Autochthonia 'putside Fate&quot; is as much, if not more so, their own existence being defined by/connected to the will of its most powerful inhabitants (Yozi, Raksha &amp; a bunch of other things, the Neverborn and Autochthon) as their being physically beyond the reach of the 5 elemental poles.<br /> <br /> Alchemicals lose flavor in what exactly? Their main complication, the &quot;charms as cybernetic implants&quot; mechanic, that makes their powerset more maleable but also more dependent on infrastructure than any other exalt, is that way <b>completely by intent</b>, a challenge/weakness built-in to reinforce their &quot;stranger in a strange land&quot; theme. The outsider, the alien out of his depth in dealing with the strange new place it has been exiled to and its challenges is <b>exactly</b> the role they are supposed to play <b>anywhere but Autochthonia</b>, be it Creation, the Wyld, Forgotten Realms, cWoD or Star Wars, so no change there - not to mention &quot;adding support infrastructure&quot; if one wants them <b>not to</b> be outsiders is not exactly a setting/system-changing addition for their sake. The only thing Alchemicals <b>might</b> actually lose wholly outside the setting would be god-machine protocols, that are indeed, afaik, wholly depedent on pattern spiders or their autochtonian equivalent hacking up the fabric of reality for them - and that depends on how that particular world stands in relation to Autochthonia in one's homebrew game.<br /> <br /> About the Fae - when did &quot;realm of chaos&quot; or &quot;world of dreams&quot; stop being a fantasy staple? Any setting with either of those two - or dreamers - is a place where the Raksha and their ilk still have ways to play their wicked narratives on the locals. Not to mention that i thought there was some kind of celestial exalt with a bunch of Wyld-only charms too, no? What were they called... moonies, lunatics, something like that, it's in the tip of the mouth but i can't seem to remember at the moment. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=158982#post158982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you <i>could</i> certainly make a setting without the concept of Fate, without colleges linked to specific star formations and have Sidereal without those elements, but you'll be cutting out a fair amount of their character and power. And the same is true for Fair Folk without the Wyld, or Alchemicals without their Vats and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Colleges as they currently stand are dross, <b>Fate filtered through skills</b> but in a less straightforward way than charms through the metaphor of the Constellations. Sidereal astrology can exist pretty fine by riffing straight into the skills per se instead, like rituals in a thaumaturgic art, for example. That said i'll agree Sidereal Astrology as presented in the previous editions has been an overly elaborate and yet hashly sketched mess of mechanics implemented in most counterintuitive ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-04-2014, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T08:20:06-07:00","id":159065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=158982#post158982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereal are tied heavily to the idea of the Loom of Fate and working to control destiny</div> </div> </div> </div>Working to control destiny, sure. A lot of settings can have concepts of destiny.<br /> <br /> What connects them to the Loom of Fate that is specific and untransplantable?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">you'd <i>also</i> have to import the entire concept of Fate</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any setting to which that is a foreign concept (except maybe for ones that are making a specific overt literary point about there being no fate)?<br /> <br /> Like, it's not exactly a unique idea to Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anubisy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compare that to Solars or Abyssals or Dragon Blooded. You can drop them into pretty much any other setting, without worrying nearly as much that their mechanics are drawing on setting material unique to Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does their Sorcery count? I feel as though their Sorcery should count.<br /> <br /> That and how Abyssals have that whole thing of different Essence respiration between Creation and the Underworld. An whatever Charms still have the Spectral Keyword.<br /> <br /> Maybe also some stuff with Solars and Holy, if one is still going with how that worked in Second Edition? I mean, I don't think it should, but just to put that out there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T08:42:29-07:00","id":159106,"title":"","content":"Just stop and look at how different Alchemical Exalted are in the Modern Shard vs how they are officially. They had to be changed rather dramatically to fit in a setting that didn't have any of the magical steampunk elements or Autochthon.<br /> <br /> If you introduce Sidereals (or Fair Folk) into a world without the setting elements that form a core part of their mechanics and themes, you'll either have to do similar rewrites to them, to strip those themes and mechanics out, or you'll have to rewrite the new setting to include the things that will allow the Sidereal or Fair Folk to work as they normally do.<br /> <br /> Again, Modern Alchemicals is the perfect example of this. You can drop many other Exalted (like Solars or Abyssals or whatever) into new settings and only need to make a few cursory changes (change out the Holy keyword, or let Abyssals regenerate motes normally). Dropping Alchemicals into a new setting requires much more profound changes (as seen in Shards), and the same is generally true for Sidereal and Fair Folk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T09:04:32-07:00","id":159116,"title":"","content":"I find myself doubting that the Modern Alchemicals had to be anything; I would expect that they were done that way mostly because it was just a neat idea, and partially just to show off how dramatically you can change an Exalt for <i>any</i> Shard. Still doesn't really matter to Sidereals, mind. You know what else The Modern Age didn't have? <i>The Celestial Bureuacracy and Loom of Fate.</i> Curiously, it did not have the least effect on the presentation of the Sidereals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T09:19:50-07:00","id":159132,"title":"","content":"Yeah, okay.<br /> <br /> You're not going to convince me that you can just drag and drop anything from Exalted into any setting without having to make any allowances at all for the way that certain splats are tied to Exalted's unique setting characteristics.<br /> <br /> Like it or not, some Exalted are, mechanically, tied more closely to certain setting elements than other Exalted, and they will suffer if you drop them into a setting without allowing for the fact that the new setting doesn't have those elements.<br /> <br /> But I don't really care enough about the topic to keep going around with you over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-04-2014, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T09:32:06-07:00","id":159138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=159106#post159106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you introduce Sidereals (or Fair Folk) into a world without the setting elements that form a core part of their mechanics and themes, you'll either have to do similar rewrites to them, to strip those themes and mechanics out, or you'll have to rewrite the new setting to include the things that will allow the Sidereal or Fair Folk to work as they normally do.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds as though you're talking specifically about astrology here. I don't know if I'd really call astrology a core part of Sidereal mechanics and themes, honestly. It,s peripheral and painful to use and it never works and they were never balanced against the assumption of having it. The experience of playing a Sidereal without access to astrology is mostly the same as playing one with access to astrology. Excising astrology from 1e or 2e (pre- or post-errata) does not have anywhere near as big an effect on Sidereals as excising certain charms, or SMA, or the cliosed-charmset. The Loom-references in the charmset, which differs from astrology in that people actually use it regularly in real games, are just minor fluff and can trivially be altered to refer to &quot;fate&quot; in a general sense without any effort or loss of functionality. Note that even Astrology is pretty easy to reskin as a generic &quot;fate manipulation&quot; power without substantive changes.<br /> <br /> Now, the near-irrelevance of Sidereal astrology is kind of dumb and should probably change, because it's stupid to add a huge flavourful subsystem that helps characterize a group's niche and then make it bad and pointless, but that's where we're at right now. That said, I would be <i>very</i> surprised if astrology ever takes a form that breaks in a serious way if you remove Heaven and the Loom from the game, because it was clearly the sort of case where they devised the Loom and astrology as somewhat discrete concepts, and then joined them at the hip for thematic reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T09:37:29-07:00","id":159143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=158982#post158982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair Folk are tied fairly heavily to the Wyld, so if you dropped them into a setting without something comparable to the Wyld, you'll again run into issues, though it's possible for them to skate by via harvesting gossamer from dreams and in 2.5 most of their charms work in Creation and the Wyld. Still, all of their Wyld-only charms would be totally useless in a setting without the Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd disagree. Fair Folk are actually very easy to work into other settings.* A Chancel is essentially a cluster of Waypoints a raksha can carry around in his pocket. Raksha who lived in the Wyld would just call those home. Chancels would naturally increase in value and importance -- as might the Charms that allow one to use a mortal's dream as a Waypoint that let them create short-lived things in Creation -- but little actually changes. Raksha who didn't engage with the Wyld much before anyway -- as indeed most of them didn't, if they're not near the edge of Creation -- are unaffected anyway.<br /> <br /> * Well, no harder than they are in the standard setting.<br /> <br /> As an aside, while Charms for creating more enduring &quot;people,&quot; artifacts, monsters, land, and the like are valuable (and accessible via the above methods), the vast majority of Wyld-Only Charms are for Shaping Combat.** And the loss of Charms for engaging in Shaping Combat can be addressed with the phrase, &quot;And nothing of value was lost.&quot; <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> ** As you noted, a raksha also learns the Waking version of the Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T10:14:34-07:00","id":159179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=159132#post159132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, okay.<br /> <br /> You're not going to convince me that you can just drag and drop anything from Exalted into any setting without having to make any allowances at all for the way that certain splats are tied to Exalted's unique setting characteristics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean his arguments haven't been convincing or that you <b>don't want</b> to be convinced, logic or lack of it notwithstanding?<br /> Because i don't mean to disrespect, but you seem to be trying to drive an opinion than actually making an argument and the rest of your post only seems to reinforce that impression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T11:51:58-07:00","id":159243,"title":"","content":"Sidereals are like private investigators, wizards, and hidden sifus: what makes them dangerous is not their own, personal strength or charisma or inherent destiny as a ruler (though they can have those things). They are dangerous because of what they <i>know</i>. Private investigators dig up secrets on evil people; wizards dig up hidden knowledge about the world itself; hidden sifus perfect inscrutable wisdom. And when they put this information to work, their enemies quake for fear of what they might do with what they know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T12:04:36-07:00","id":159268,"title":"","content":"On reflection, I think Shards' Alchemicals were the <i>only</i> case where a splat required appreciable mechanical tweaks to work in a published shard, ignoring Burn Legend. This reflects the fact that Alchemicals need vat complexes, both in a crunch and fluff sense, in a way that nobody else in the setting needs anything. Like, if the only way Sidereals could learn new Charms was to to go to the Loom and help College-appropriate Pattern Spiders weave Fate (in a way with mechanically explicit requirements) in order to coax the spiders into teaching them the Charm, that would begin to approach the level of dependency Alchemicals have on vats. Even then, though, the role that vat complexes serve <i>in the setting</i> is not particularly important to the effect they have on the Alchemical splat, nor is Autochtonia as a whole, which is why it wasn't that much work to just substitute a different mechanism that functioned similarly and had totally different fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T12:10:56-07:00","id":159273,"title":"","content":"Sidereals without the setting trappings, which is to say distilled to their roots, owe a lot to <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angels_in_Judaism\" target=\"_blank\">Angels</a> and other enactors-of-the-will-of-the-divine counterparts in other mythologies. Assuming for a moment a layer of abstraction between the myths-as-recorded and the actual mechanisms, one could for example say that it wasn't Mercury himself who visited Aeneas in Carthage, but a Chosen of Journeys masquerating as same. Ditto Eris at the banquet and a Chosen of Battles, or the Flaming Sword guarding Eden and a Chosen of Endings.<br /> <br /> The Sidereal power set answers the question, &quot;what if those forces were people?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 06-04-2014, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T17:13:36-07:00","id":159458,"title":"","content":"I think there's some serious confusion in this thread with Sidereal astrology and the Loom of Fate. The Loom exists to explain how Sidereal astrology works not the other way around. Sidereal astrology could just as easily have been written to work through other means, the Loom was just the one that got chosen in the end. Removing the Loom from the setting doesn't really change much for Sidereal game mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T18:22:07-07:00","id":159581,"title":"","content":"To quote Hatewheel, Sidereals are &quot;agents of the mythos&quot;. What does this mean?<br /> <br /> When an angel comes down from Heaven to wrestle Jacob, he's an agent of the mythos.<br /> <br /> When Pythia gives Heracles his penance, she's an agent of the mythos.<br /> <br /> When Buddha subdues Sun Wukong, he's an agent of the mythos.<br /> <br /> (Jacob and Heracles are Solar archetypes, Sun Wukong is clearly a Lunar. Though I guess arguments could be made for Jacob being a Dragon-Blooded, given his role as a progenitor of a chosen nation.)<br /> <br /> Agents of the mythos act on behalf of a greater power (Hebrew God, Greek Pantheon, Chinese Heavens, respectively) to test the hero, give him direction and guidance, and to uphold proper order of the world. They act as antagonists as often as they act as mentors and advisers.<br /> <br /> It's a common archetype, easily found in almost every setting. What's important, though, is that outside of their story roles, angels, oracles and Buddha don't have much in common in terms of powers and outlook - those are intimately tied to the mythos they represent, whereas a hero's (Solar's) role is to approach the mythos from the more common human perspective.<br /> <br /> In other words, while a Sidereal wouldn't be entirely out of place in a different setting due to common story roles, his powers would feel out of place, because they are pretty closely tied to him being an agent of Fate, Maidens and Heaven, in the sense Exalted uses those words, with all the baggage it entails. This is a feature, not a bug.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T19:12:37-07:00","id":159603,"title":"","content":"Alchemicals in the Modern shard absolutely didn't need to be the Modern versions. They could have been cyborg agents and slaves of the Infernal Exalted, created and supported by the Infernal's mortal mad scientist minions. But the Infernals already have the Terrestrials, Sidereals and Lunars serving them, and &quot;rogue cyborg&quot; is a more player-friendly game when the cyborg can operate independently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T19:53:01-07:00","id":159661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=159581#post159581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other words, while a Sidereal wouldn't be entirely out of place in a different setting due to common story roles, his powers would feel out of place, because they are pretty closely tied to him being an agent of Fate, Maidens and Heaven, in the sense Exalted uses those words, with all the baggage it entails. This is a feature, not a bug.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bI'd say that Exalted's kitchen sink approach to the setting makes adapting charm sets to a change like this fairly easy. Shards didn't have to do much for its adjustments. Rewriting fluff isn't very difficult in my experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T22:16:03-07:00","id":159751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=159179#post159179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does that mean his arguments haven't been convincing or that you <b>don't want</b> to be convinced, logic or lack of it notwithstanding?<br /> Because i don't mean to disrespect, but you seem to be trying to drive an opinion than actually making an argument and the rest of your post only seems to reinforce that impression.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's because I completely fail to understand how people feel that some of the Exalted splats <i>don't</i> have ties to certain elements that are fairly unique to Exalted, and that taking those characters and placing them in a setting without those elements will require you to either ignore segments of that Exalted splat, or modify either the new setting or the Exalted in order to make up for it.<br /> <br /> Lift up Alchemicals and drop them into say, Conan the Barbarian. You're going to need to either modify the Alchemicals so that they don't need all of their magical steampunk infrastructure, or you're going to have to modify Hyboria to have the magical steampunk infrastructure that Alchemicals require to operate.<br /> <br /> If you drop the Sidereal Exalted into Rifts Earth, you're going to either need to remove the concept of Fate from their charms, as well as Astrology effects, or you'll need to modify the setting so that it does have Fate and has Astrology based around those various Colleges, or you'll have to modify how Sidereal Astrology/Fate-stuff works in the absence of a Loom of Fate.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't know how there's any kind of debate about this. I've run lots of cross overs using many systems, and when you come across certain character types who are tied to a setting more strongly than others, you have to make allowances and modifications when you place them in a new setting.<br /> <br /> That's like, basic crossover 101. Some stuff is tied more strongly to unique setting elements than other stuff. So I'm just surprised that so many people seem to disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-05-2014, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T01:23:06-07:00","id":159806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Buddha subdues Sun Wukong, he's an agent of the mythos.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Buddha is a Solar; the Jade Emperor who turned to him for assistance when his own methods failed is the Sidereal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T01:42:04-07:00","id":159809,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't know how there's any kind of debate about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the things you're describing are about as integral as the Incarnae are, and yet apparently you can envision Solars and Lunars and the like in other settings without adding an Unconquered Sun or Luna to choose them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=159751#post159751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you drop the Sidereal Exalted into Rifts Earth, you're going to either need to remove the concept of Fate from their charms</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, why; why is the broad concept of &quot;fate&quot;, as has existed in actual cultures for thousands of years, incompatible with these settings to the point that it's invalid as a description for how these Charms work? If you're ever playing in a Rifts game and some NPC makes a reference to the idea of fate, do you have your character respond with confusion or argument?<br /> <br /> Secondly, okay, remove Fate. &quot;Hey, how does Wise Choice work?&quot; &quot;Seeing the future.&quot; &quot;Oh, makes sense.&quot; What exactly is the enormous gap that needs to be filled?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">as well as Astrology effects</div> </div> </div> </div>And Astrology can't just be a causality modifying magic based around a coherent set of symbols because...?<br /> <br /> Hell, in the actual Sidereals material, they hardly even call the Colleges &quot;constellations&quot;, so one doesn't even need to get hung up that their symbols aren't literally images that can be made from stars in the sky.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they can, since those patterns are pretty vague anyway. &quot;Oh look, a bunch of stars in a kind of triangular formation. Looks kind of like a goat mermaid, don't it?&quot; Really, &quot;the Mask&quot; would serve as a pretty decent alternate name for Capricorn anyway, so there's that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">you'll have to modify how Sidereal Astrology/Fate-stuff works in the absence of a Loom of Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does it work with the <i>presence</i> of a Loom of Fate?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm just going to reiterate that not only does The Modern Age not contain a Loom of Fate, but the Shards Simple Astrology rules explicitly label themselves as something to use in a setting with no Loom of Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-05-2014, 04:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T01:45:18-07:00","id":159810,"title":"","content":"I'll note, I'm caught up in this argument just as a matter of not seeing logical cohesion; as far as I can tell, Thoth's original point was about relocating Sidereals from within the same setting, so the ideas of crossover and stuff doesn't really matter to it.<br /> <br /> Although that original point doesn't really have much to discuss about anyway, if I'm reading it correctly. &quot;Take away their elders and gods and stuff, and where's the Siderealness?&quot; Right in Easily Accepted Proposition Stance, person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T01:57:32-07:00","id":159818,"title":"","content":"Unless you find some replacement... a group of boring dudes with unwieldy power trees that are highly comprised of nonsequitors, basically. <br /> <br /> The entire interest of playing a Sidereal is in their Agent role. A Sidereal doesn't work for himself, he works for something bigger than himself. Remove the higher purpose and the organizational themes and all you get is some dudes with annoying to use for no reason power sets that look made by someone high on some narcotic. <br /> <br /> And I say this as someone who coniders Sidereals his favorite splat to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T02:39:56-07:00","id":159844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=159806#post159806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Buddha is a Solar; the Jade Emperor who turned to him for assistance when his own methods failed is the Sidereal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Buddha is an enlightened teacher whose power over reality comes from having seen the true nature of it, and he defeats Sun Wukong with a cosmos-warping paradox. If that doesn't scream &quot;Sidereal&quot;, I don't know what does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T08:29:45-07:00","id":159999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=159818#post159818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you find some replacement... a group of boring dudes with unwieldy power trees that are highly comprised of nonsequitors, basically.<br /> <br /> The entire interest of playing a Sidereal is in their Agent role. A Sidereal doesn't work for himself, he works for something bigger than himself. Remove the higher purpose and the organizational themes and all you get is some dudes with annoying to use for no reason power sets that look made by someone high on some narcotic.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are mistaking &quot;the entire interest of playing a Sidereal&quot; for &quot;my entire interest of playing a Sidereal&quot;. A sidereal fan who doesn't like their mechanics, and is only into them for the &quot;agent&quot; role and its associated trappings, is an atypical Sidereal fan, and not the kind of person the splat was designed for. A Ronin Sidereal is closer to the Sidereal essence than that Getimian sig we heard about who happens to be doing the job of a Sidereal.<br /> <br /> Judging from what you're saying here, I think you would be happier playing a member of the Cult of the Illuminated or the All-Seeing Eye, rather than being unhappy as a Sidereal just for the sake of that niche. Certainly, you should avoid projecting your distate for their powerset -- and, to be perfectly frank, your inability to understand it -- on all Sidereal fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T10:05:23-07:00","id":160045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=159844#post159844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Buddha is an enlightened teacher whose power over reality comes from having seen the true nature of it, and he defeats Sun Wukong with a cosmos-warping paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be looking at him more from the perspective of an ostensibly normal guy whose sense of perspective makes him somebody who gods and demons flock to in order to deal with a problem beyond any of them.<br /> <br /> And for that whole &quot;the pillars of the earth are my fingers&quot; trick to be a high-Essence Lore Charm.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T10:39:17-07:00","id":160058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=160045#post160045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be looking at him more from the perspective of an ostensibly normal guy whose sense of perspective makes him somebody who gods and demons flock to in order to deal with a problem beyond any of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds more like Sidereal territory to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T10:41:09-07:00","id":160059,"title":"","content":"You get Rakan Thulio.<br /> <br /> A Sidereal not employed by heaven is someone with the power and freedom to radically reshape the existing system, including tearing it down. No wonder Sidereals are identified, kidnapped and trained since birth: every unindoctrinated Seer has the potential to be an existential threat to heaven.<br /> <br /> Try running a group of ronin Sidereals, either as PCs or as antagonists, as a cell of reality bending terrorists or revolutionaries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T10:42:52-07:00","id":160063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=159806#post159806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Buddha is a Solar; the Jade Emperor who turned to him for assistance when his own methods failed is the Sidereal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I... That's perfect...<br /> <br /> You have just made the Zenith caste make COMPLETE SENSE to me for the first time since I started playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T11:21:17-07:00","id":160105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=160058#post160058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds more like Sidereal territory to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals are weird the way gods are weird. They're not people who partake of the idea that they're supposed to be normal, the way Solars are.<br /> <br /> ... Shit, I thought of an analogy that conveys my perspective on the thing, but it feels dreadfully appropriating and condescending, so I don't really want to say it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T11:25:10-07:00","id":160106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=160059#post160059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No wonder Sidereals are identified, kidnapped and trained since birth</div> </div> </div> </div>But they aren't. I mean, they are trained since birth, in a subtle, Sidereal manner. But they don't bust into people's houses and raid their cribs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not that I know of anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T12:46:00-07:00","id":160155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=159999#post159999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are mistaking &quot;the entire interest of playing a Sidereal&quot; for &quot;my entire interest of playing a Sidereal&quot;. A sidereal fan who doesn't like their mechanics, and is only into them for the &quot;agent&quot; role and its associated trappings, is an atypical Sidereal fan, and not the kind of person the splat was designed for. A Ronin Sidereal is closer to the Sidereal essence than that Getimian sig we heard about who happens to be doing the job of a Sidereal.<br /> <br /> Judging from what you're saying here, I think you would be happier playing a member of the Cult of the Illuminated or the All-Seeing Eye, rather than being unhappy as a Sidereal just for the sake of that niche. Certainly, you should avoid projecting your distate for their powerset -- and, to be perfectly frank, your inability to understand it -- on all Sidereal fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gee. <i>That </i>sure doesn't sound horribly self-satisfied and smug. Thanks for reminding me of my wrongness.<br /> <br /> I understand the powers plenty, don't you worry. They are not in any way complex. But without the background of being part of the godly hierarchy and envoys of the maidens and agents to make things go as they should and so on? A lot of them would make a shitload less sense. Like, let's take something very simple to not get lost in particulars and pedantry. I dunno, Medicine. Sidereal Medicine kills zombies instead of helping keep and continue life (which is what Medicine is ostensibly for) as an expression of Saturn's purview of Endings - an Endings Sidereal was chosen to make sure that things die in the proper way, he was not chosen to keep life, that is not what his basic job is, and Saturn's magic is not going to help him do that, so deal. You remove &quot;being designed to do the job for Saturn&quot; from the equation, and what you get is a bunch of guys who seem to be unable to use medicine to actually help anyone for no real reason other than, ostensibly, some designer feeling like being cute and making the Charm tree a nonsequitor from the Ability.<br /> <br /> And for the record? I'm plenty happy playing Sidereals. They get the coolest background, an actual place in the setting instead of the whole &quot;you're a returned king and should rule&quot; thing that annoys me to the marrow of my bones, limits and rules and organizations to uphold and work around, they get almost the only magic powers in the game that actually feel like magic, and trying to succeed when your Charmset is a grab bag of magic spells that half the time have nothing to do with the task at hand is fun. But I know perfectly well why I enjoy them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","user":"Drascin","date":". 06-05-2014, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T12:56:55-07:00","id":160163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=160105#post160105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals are weird the way gods are weird. They're not people who partake of the idea that they're supposed to be normal, the way Solars are..</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like Buddha, who claimed he was neither man nor god?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T14:17:32-07:00","id":160248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=160106#post160106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they aren't. I mean, they are trained since birth, in a subtle, Sidereal manner. But they don't bust into people's houses and raid their cribs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not that I know of anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Why am I reminded of Wizard People, Dear Reader?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T17:51:59-07:00","id":160415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=160155#post160155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gee. <i>That </i>sure doesn't sound horribly self-satisfied and smug. Thanks for reminding me of my wrongness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals have the best-designed powerset in 1e. Maybe the best-designed powerset in the history of the line. It is a major component of what people who like Sidereals like about Sidereals. Presenting it as though it's random and aimless is insulting to those people <i>while also</i> giving the sense that you don't really grok the splat. It's difficult to be wholly inoffensive about expressing that, and given the tone of your original post, probably not worth the effort.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=160155#post160155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand the powers plenty, don't you worry. They are not in any way complex.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are not doing a good job of convincing me of this!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=160155#post160155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But without the background of being part of the godly hierarchy and envoys of the maidens and agents to make things go as they should and so on? A lot of them would make a shitload less sense. Like, let's take something very simple to not get lost in particulars and pedantry. I dunno, Medicine. Sidereal Medicine kills zombies instead of helping keep and continue life (which is what Medicine is ostensibly for) as an expression of Saturn's purview of Endings - an Endings Sidereal was chosen to make sure that things die in the proper way, he was not chosen to keep life, that is not what his basic job is, and Saturn's magic is not going to help him do that, so deal. You remove &quot;being designed to do the job for Saturn&quot; from the equation, and what you get is a bunch of guys who seem to be unable to use medicine to actually help anyone for no real reason other than, ostensibly, some designer feeling like being cute and making the Charm tree a nonsequitor from the Ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're correct that Sidereal Medicine is clearly filtered through the lens of Endings, but it's a mistake to infer that it's because of the &quot;job&quot;. Notice that the closest charmset to Sidereals' in terms of what goes where is the Dragon-Blooded one, which is the absolute antithesis of &quot;you were chosen as this caste in order to do your patron's job for them.&quot; Dragon-Blooded Thrown doesn't give you a tornado shield because Mela wants you to go around tornading things. But the dragon-blooded charmset is also full of &quot;non sequiturs&quot;, by which you seem to mean &quot;effects that don't flow logically from the mundane application of the Ability&quot;. It's more noticeable in Sidereals because they get fewer general-purpose effects, but that's part of the unrelated design goals of giving them a small number of charms and ensuring that their access to core meat-and-potatoes effects is limited. Once you rule out Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded, the <i>only</i> Ability Exalted left over are Solars (for whom &quot;fairly literal application of the Ability&quot; is a core thematic), and Abyssals (whose charmset is a very close relative of the Solars'). From the 3e Infernals preview, it looks like Ability Infernals lean a lot more in the Sidereal direction.<br /> <br /> If I were going to try to put my finger on the essence of the esoteric nature of Sidereal charms -- thematically, I mean, beyond just the &quot;they're kind of scattered to force you to tap-dance&quot;, which you're absolutely right about -- it would be down to two things:<ul><li>Unlike most Exalted, Sidereals get different portions of their charmset from different gods. The Endings charms aren't Saturn-themed because they're hints about what Saturn expects you to go do, they're Saturn-themed because <i>the charms of Saturn express the nature of Saturn</i>, much like the charms of Luna express the nature of Luna.</li> <li>Sidereals develop in power by building an enlightened understanding of the cosmos, as filtered through the Colleges (and, implicitly, through the minds of the Maidens). Their powers are often metaphorical because each one is representing 1/25th of the entire nature of the universe, as embodied in the associated scripture. A Sidereal who progresses through the Medicine tree uses her knowledge of Medicine to develop a transcendent understanding of the purview of the Corpse, because secret cosmic wisdom and enlightenment are Sidereal themes.</li> </ul><br /> It's a disservice to the charmset and the people responsible for it to suggest that this was an arbitrary or careless decision, or that the choices made were not made carefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 06-06-2014, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T17:53:37-07:00","id":160417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=160248#post160248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Why am I reminded of Wizard People, Dear Reader?</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://img.4plebs.org/boards/tg/image/1387/59/1387590102594.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T19:41:03-07:00","id":161349,"title":"","content":"Over in Spacebattles, I and a poster called Ryuugi got to talking about, &quot;In Kingdom Hearts, what if the original Keyblade went to Riku as it was intended, and Sora instead received an Exaltation?&quot;<br /> <br /> Ryuugi decided to explore the idea of Sora as a Sidereal Exalt. These are his thoughts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Premise</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Destiny Islands are being torn apart and consumed by Darkness. Without any kind of weapon to fight the Heartless, Chosen of [Journeys / Battles / Serenity] Sora beats the ever-loving shit out of them with his bare fists, until there's no more world left to stand on, and he falls through a dark void lit by all the stars of the universe.<br /> <br /> Afterwards, he awakens in a strange place. Moreover, something strange is going on; most people barely notice him, and when he departs their presence they forget him entirely. In time, he learns his fate -- to be forgotten by the world, forgotten by anyone he meets, forgotten by the very friends he strives to protect, but yet possessing the power he needs to save them all. He finds paths between worlds in a realm they call Heaven, learns of the fate that awaits the ones he loves if he does nothing, and travels the universe to save them.<br /> <br /> Kairi is awake and alive, but hunted in worlds far from her own. Riku is walking a path fraught with dangers within and without, against which his Keyblade is as much bait as defense. So Sora, whom neither remembers, chases after both knowing that its worth it as long as he can keep them safe.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Arcane Fate and Kairi</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I prefer to retain the Storytelling potential of the Arcane Fate, due to the effect it has on the character dynamics. Not only is it a tragedy for Sora--one Kairi doesn't even remember--but its not enough to stop him from aiding her however he can. He'll protect his friend, follow her to the ends of the Universe and aid her silently, even if she doesn't and might never remember who he is.<br /> <br /> Why? Because she's his friend and he loves her.<br /> <br /> There's also Kairi's side of things, with a part of her life so cruelly torn away and she can't even remember how. Have you seen...what was it? Season Five of Doctor who? When Rory vanishes and Amy can't remember him and yet sometimes someone would ask something and she wouldn't remember but she'd cry? And what Rory did when he returned.<br /> <br /> Kairi doesn't remember Sora--can't remember him--but she keeps meeting this boy who wants to help her and though she can't recall his name and never things of him when he's gone, he's...<br /> <br /> There's a lot of potential on both sides in the face of what's been forgotten.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Being A Sidereal</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">If Sora became a Sidereal, right off the bat that means a bunch of different things. It means everyone he knows--and almost everyone he meets--will forget him. Evidence and memories of his existence would fade away like dust in the wind. He could walk up to Kairi or Riku and they wouldn't know him, baring use of magic. But it also means he'd have a lot of power, most of which doesn't involve fighting at all, because a large part of being a Sid is avoiding combat or making it so you don't need to fight. It gives him a diverse set of useful powers to take advantage of, but also imposes a lot of limits as he has to act within the bounds of his Charmset. There's also the involvement of enhanced knowledge such as from the various prediction effects Sidereals have and their roundabout way of doing things.<br /> <br /> To be a Sidereal is to be forgotten. Even his closest friends forget him, and though massive time and effort could leave impressions, even they won't think of him when he's gone. Those he meets, fights for, and saves--they forget him when he leaves. He has no Keyblade to save the worlds, no destiny there. He is a hero, but no one anyone knows about. And yet, he devotes himself to saving them anyway, to do as much as he can to bring happiness to the world, and trying with all his power to help and support Kairi and Riku.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>The Plot</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">My rough picture of things going to relate things broadly to Xehanort's plan, perhaps taking place in a situation roughly analogous to Hollow Bastion in the First Game and the whole Riku fight/freeing of Kairi's heart and so on. Xehanort's canonically spent plenty of time in the Dark Margin and found the Jade Prison in his efforts and began to slowly work to extract them from it one by one and slowly converting them into Abyssals. He then plugs and plays with eligible targets who fit specific criteria--such as the Organization Members, I was thinking, though with a number of design changes from the canon model, a number of which Xehanort couldn't predict and isn't aware of.<br /> <br /> After Riku got sufficiently corrupted by the Darkness but after he still got kicked to the curb in a climactic fight with... I'm thinking Kairi and her friends (maybe or maybe not including Sora), a shard is attracted to him and he makes the deal with Ansem and becomes an Abyssal. Insert Round 2, but this time it's against a Solaroid who chose to be a huge dick and dump everything into Melee so he could block all your fucking attacks and hit like a motherfucker and thank god for Olympia--ahem. So round two with Riku--or Riku suffering from a sort of Past Lives/Urge/Resonance hybrid, at least--starts and it doesn't go so hot. Fighting a Solar-tier Melee focused Exalt in a sword fight, even a young one, is an enormous pain even with a sweet Keyblade--especially since Riku also has a Keyblade of his own*. The good guys get the ever loving shit beaten out of them until Sora steps in to fight directly, at which point Riku starts remembering him directly, but the fight still doesn't go so well, because Keyword defenses fuck with a lot of Sora's non-lethal Martial Arts and while he can fight him and hurt him, he can't bring himself to go far enough to risk killing his friend--and Abyssals can be tricky bitches about going down besides, especially while on an Exaltation high, in armor, and being fed Xehanort-brand steroids.<br /> <br /> The bright side is that seeing Sora and Riku fight finally begins wearing on the Arcane Fate some and Kairi finally manages to get that first or second dot-worth of Acquaintance and remembers Sora's name. Insert emotional reunion, insert Abyssals being dicks and ruining parties they didn't get invited to, insert return to action sequence. Kairi's wondering if there's any way to win with her lacking an Exaltation and Sora admits to having had visions (Source: Sidereal Lore/Investigation/Awareness/a prayer roll to the Maidens) of someplace he knew it was his destiny to travel to. Kairi opts to face Riku alone while Sora runs past him to do Sidereal business, Yellow Pathing his way to timeliness. Kairi opens the Keyhole and Sora rushes through the Door to Darkness and then into the Realm of Darkness. He locates the Jade Prison and opens it.<br /> <br /> Up top, Kairi gets a major dose of shine goodness. Down low, Sora finishes grinding to the next level and levels up to Essence 5--though I've also been contemplating Oathkeeper/Oblivion given their thematic importance to Sora by representing Kairi and Riku, the dual nature of his heart, and their general coolness. Excrement becomes actualized and the Keyhole is closed with Sora on one side and Kairi and Riku on the other, ending the arc.<br /> <br /> Vague thoughts following that: Sora's locked in eternal darkness. Are you a bad enough dude to rescue the Chosen of Fate?<br /> <br /> *And tell me Souleater isn't an Abyssal weapon?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Sora's power-set</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Charms of Serenity are especially well equipped for a role of shadowing and supporting someone else--especially Craft, Dodge, and Linguistics, though Performance and Socialize are by no means lacking either. With MA favored and some of the other vital parts of Sidereal Wise Mastering--like Lore, for instance, and Awareness--and he'd be in a great position to guide his friends through the minefields that are their lives, while also having to make things work.<br /> <br /> Add in some astrology...<br /> <br /> I have a good idea of which Styles I want--Throne Shadow for obvious reasons and probably Sapphire Veil later on, also for obvious reasons*. My main question is twofold: Does he need any other styles? Beyond some dabbling, which is periodically useful; a number of Styles have some useful tech hidden in them that can be used. But any specific styles you think should be dabbled in or etc. In all honesty, I avoid Scroll of the Monk and the Dragon-Blooded book like they'll give me testicular cancer by proximity.<br /> <br /> And second of all, I wanted to get a take on what you guys think about Essence? I'm sure about him either starting at three or reaching it very quickly, but because of the pain in the as of raising Essence, I'm wondering whether to just start him higher (between the...god, three Hearts inside him? It's not hard to hand wave up to 4), whether I should start at three and sort of handwave some of the rules, or use the 3E version of appropriate moments. I'm leaning toward the later, though I suppose a mix of options could work, too.<br /> <br /> *But just in case it's not obvious: Throne Shadow is the Sidereal's Hero Style and is the only MA style they can make Charms for. Which also makes it the only part of their Charmset they can make Charms for, period. Sapphire Veil of Passion Style, meanwhile, is a Sidereal MA Style that's 1) not mechanically broken, 2) not broken mechanically, and 3) at a low enough Essence that it actually has a place in the setting since non-Elders can by it. Even with the Charm that allows Sids to buy Essence 6 MA Charms I think there are, like, two other SMAs that can be completed without being a hundred years old. Which is a big deal, because you need to complete SMA styles to get the Master Sutra that lets you not spend your entire motepool in one Charm.<br /> <br /> But actually, I'd given thought to the Virtue Styles and they do fit. They're good styles--showing their age some and missing a few major bits that have sense been added, but again, that's every MA--and they also make thematic sense. It can be easy to miss, but Virtues are supposed to be very central to Sids; while they don't have an mote-pool expansion Charms, this was by design. They were supposed to use (Virtue) Essence Replenishment as a replacement; having a technically lower mote pool but being able to potentially generate a theoretical max of two hundred additional motes via obeying their virtues--which is also why they're paired with the Virtue Keyword, that makes a lot of Charms open to Virtue channeling.<br /> <br /> (Of course, this got messed up in practice because the writers of Sids didn't know what they were doing, but...)<br /> <br /> It's also a very good match for Sora, who's a very Virtuous character. While Compassion, Conviction, and Valor are obvious, he even shows a lot of temperance, such as when he refuses to go back to the Islands--what he wants most--until he finds the King and Riku and the many other times he resists temptation.<br /> <br /> Given the importance of Virtues to both Sora and to Sidereals, playing with that could work well, and the Virtue Styles are very powerful.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Yu-Shan</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Though speaking of Heaven, I've also be thinking about where it fits. My take on it was to merge the cosmologies--Creation was the original world that was broken apart. Heaven still exists though, connected to all the other worlds via it's original connection to Creation. Something I've been pondering, though, is how it's changed? Certainly, there would be a lot of new gods for the new cities, worlds, places, and things, but how many of the Exalted Gods should remain approximately the same? It makes sense in a lot of ways, as you'd figure that being in a position of strength before the fracture would equip them to better wrangle for a new position, but what do you guys think?<br /> <br /> If it came up, I could see Kairi and Riku Exalting later in the story as a Solar and Abyssal respectively. The Abyssals would need to get a different background, of course, but they actually work pretty well with the mechanics of the Heartless, allowing for sufficiently special circumstances. That could be pretty cool, potentially, but I'm not sure if it'd be a good idea; while by the time it came up, Sora would be Essence 5 to their 2 or 3, there remains the potential for overshadowing. On the other hand, that could be cool in and off itself--Sidereals work best in the shadows and he'd play the role of the wise old master, while also protecting them from the shadows and guiding them. And really, the more I think about it, it kind of seems fitting, though it might just be me.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T20:42:28-07:00","id":161382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=160106#post160106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they aren't. I mean, they are trained since birth, in a subtle, Sidereal manner. But they don't bust into people's houses and raid their cribs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not that I know of anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course not. That would be wrong. So Sidereals never do it.<br /> <br /> ...well, <i>almost</i> never. I mean, if it's for the good of Creation, then they would do it. But not under any other circumstances.<br /> <br /> ...of course, when I say <i>almost</i> never, I mean <i>hardly</i> ever. And not <i>recently</i>, of course.<br /> <br /> ...recently by the standards of people who live for thousands of years, I mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T23:42:17-07:00","id":161454,"title":"","content":"This is why people hate Sidereals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T16:44:55-07:00","id":166341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/158482-who-are-the-sidereals-without-the-setting?p=161382#post161382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course not. That would be wrong. So Sidereals never do it.<br /> <br /> ...well, <i>almost</i> never. I mean, if it's for the good of Creation, then they would do it. But not under any other circumstances.<br /> <br /> ...of course, when I say <i>almost</i> never, I mean <i>hardly</i> ever. And not <i>recently</i>, of course.<br /> <br /> ...recently by the standards of people who live for thousands of years, I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on the circumstances, probably.<br /> <br /> Inserting a mentor into an existing environment is a lot more efficient than trying to create a completely new one, after all, and a healthy and supportive family life as a child is highly conducive to stable adult personalities. So kidnapping future Sidereals for brainwashing as a matter of course would be stupid. And not the smart-person-really-missed-a-trick stupid that Sids are prone to, <i>stupid</i>-stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"